WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.230
“Congratulations!

2
00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.730
You’ve won ten thousand game diamonds.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.280
Just log in here before midnight.”

4
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.780
A student showed me this yesterday.

5
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.620
Diamonds, a deadline and a login page.

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.360
I’ve seen this film before.

7
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.780
Today: how to spot a scam before it

8
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.960
catches you, and what to do next.

9
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.030
A scam is a message that tries to

10
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.050
trick you into clicking, paying, or

11
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.170
giving away a password or a code.

12
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.640
Scammers go where young people are: game

13
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.880
chats, social media, texts and WhatsApp.

14
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.680
They use the games, the stars

15
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.080
and the prizes you like.

16
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.200
Watch for five warning signs.

17
00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.450
It’s too good to be true.

18
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:52.950
It hurries you.

19
00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.110
It asks for a code, a password or money.

20
00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.690
It has a link you didn’t expect.

21
00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:01.970
And the sender isn’t who

22
00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:02.790
they say they are.

23
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.660
Look at the diamonds message again.

24
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.040
Ten thousand free diamonds:

25
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:09.740
too good to be true.

26
00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.990
Before midnight: a hurry.

27
00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:15.310
The login page isn’t the game’s own app,

28
00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:17.350
and that’s where they steal your password.

29
00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.380
Other scams aimed at young people: “free

30
00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.480
followers” that need your password.

31
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:27.100
Giveaways that want a small delivery fee.

32
00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:29.890
Easy money jobs that pass

33
00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.130
money through your account.

34
00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:34.350
And online shops with prices far too

35
00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.150
low, that want payment first.

36
00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.750
So here’s the habit.

37
00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:42.790
Stop: don’t tap, reply or pay.

38
00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.870
Check another way: open the official app

39
00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.210
yourself, or ask a trusted adult.

40
00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:50.830
A real prize will still be

41
00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:51.870
there after you check.

42
00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:53.590
Quick check!

43
00:01:54.230 --> 00:01:57.490
A text says: “Free ten gigabytes of data!

44
00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:01.370
Tap here and enter your number and PIN.”

45
00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:03.650
Scam or safe?

46
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:05.520
Scam.

47
00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.950
No real phone company asks for your PIN,

48
00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.350
and a free gift that needs it isn’t free.

49
00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:15.030
Your PIN is for you alone.

50
00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.090
Spotted one?

51
00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.420
Don’t argue with the scammer: report it

52
00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:22.780
with the app’s report button, block the

53
00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.560
sender and warn your friends.

54
00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.000
Clicked or paid by mistake?

55
00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.350
Tell a trusted adult straight away: the

56
00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.110
sooner, the more can be saved.

57
00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.310
Being tricked doesn’t make you

58
00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.990
stupid: scammers do this all day.

59
00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:38.950
Your turn.

60
00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:43.070
A shop on social media sells new phones

61
00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.430
at half price, but you must pay by

62
00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.010
mobile money first, today only.

63
00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:50.830
What do you do?

64
00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:56.070
Don’t pay: half price, pay first and

65
00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.710
today only are three warning signs.

66
00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:03.490
Remember: spot the sign, stop, check

67
00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.110
another way, then report and tell.

68
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.650
Try it tomorrow: look through the messages

69
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:12.470
on your phone, or a family phone with

70
00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.070
permission, and find one with a warning

71
00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:15.430
sign.

72
00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.720
Show it to someone at home, and

73
00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.640
